{"id": "EUVD-2026-58901", "enisaUuid": "22355489-552d-376c-800b-0e61dc116a9f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: ISST: Restore SST-PP control to all domains\n\nThe SST-PP control offset is only restored to power domain 0 after\nresume. During suspend, control values are read and stored for all\npower domains.\n\nUse pd_info->sst_base instead of power_domain_info->sst_base, which\nonly points to power domain 0 base address.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:53:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:44:58", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cea03d67db3a880893360bdbb1b0b8d9b33b1799", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a42f651cce91e9cbe65fe933622c522cbb1868b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2565a28cdcdcb035e151d285efcba26bccb3726e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72143", "GHSA-cqvm-rfr6-chr5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "154f57c3-a984-3ae8-b2bd-eae5bacffc0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc7901b5a1563a9c9eb29b3b0b0dac3162065cd8 <2a42f651cce91e9cbe65fe933622c522cbb1868b"}, {"id": "2d79be49-aa19-3e5c-bc45-b5ce0c4f0f73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc7901b5a1563a9c9eb29b3b0b0dac3162065cd8 <2565a28cdcdcb035e151d285efcba26bccb3726e"}, {"id": "33648724-a94a-314e-8c9e-b2bccc16e9b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "476c734a-b5a3-34e4-8e3d-3d127fd4ec02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3704ce5d7156ee837461be99841f312c64700b0 <cea03d67db3a880893360bdbb1b0b8d9b33b1799"}, {"id": "4c4968d7-329e-3573-aa59-c6c9b7a14bff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2624f3bf45a830cb3b8c8b967b23a72139700562"}, {"id": "6bf3